{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "חטאת הקהל הוא", :translit "chatat ha-kahal hu", :gloss "a sin-offering of the congregation it is"} {:he "אשר נשיא יחטא", :translit "asher nasi yecheta", :gloss "when a nasi sins"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah: two adjacent verses placed in juxtaposition to derive a moral principle"}], :frame {:text "The principle that one who can protest wrongdoing and fails to do so is held accountable appears in Shabbat 54b: \"Whoever can protest to his household and does not, is held accountable for his household; to the people of his city and does not, is held accountable for the people of his city; to the whole world and does not, is held accountable for the whole world.\" The Ba'al HaTurim derives this from the juxtaposition of Leviticus 4:21, which speaks of the congregation's sin, with Leviticus 4:22, which speaks of the nasi's sin.", :sources ["Shabbat 54b" "Leviticus 4:21" "Leviticus 4:22"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah: two adjacent verses placed in juxtaposition to derive a moral principle", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:45.770428131Z", :model "glm-5.2"}